{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the man took a golden ring.</b> The sage R. Moses interprets this verse according to its plain sense: ״ויקח האיש נזם זהב ושני צמידים בידו״ — to give them upon her if she prove worthy, and he said to her: ״Whose daughter are you?״ And when she told him her family, then he gave them to her. And the verse shortened its words, as we find in several places. And thus he proves from the account of his words, where it is written ״ואשאל״ and afterwards ״ואשים״. And also here it is not written ״ויקח האיש נזם זהב ויתן על ידה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:54.899793682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}